# Line endings and file types.
#
# This asks git for LF line endings on text files, so a checkout on Windows
# cannot quietly turn a plugin file into CRLF and hand a Zen Cart store a file
# that differs byte-for-byte from the one that was tested.
* text=auto eol=lf

# THE PDFs MUST BE BINARY.
#
# Not a precaution - git gets this one wrong here. Its heuristic calls a file
# text when the first 8000 bytes hold no NUL byte, and both sign-up sheets are
# hand-built with an UNCOMPRESSED content stream, so they are almost entirely
# ASCII and contain no NUL at all. Left to that heuristic git offers to "fix"
# their line endings, which rewrites bytes inside the file and shifts every
# offset in its cross-reference table. The result is a PDF that viewers
# refuse to open, produced by nothing more than cloning the repository on a
# different platform.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
